# Compiling an example or exercise to try it (`bpp examples/ch01/foo.bpp -o foo`)
# drops an extensionless native binary in the book tree. Keep only the book's
# sources — prose (.md), B++ listings (.bpp), the test runner (.sh), and this
# file — and ignore everything else (compiled binaries, .bug maps, junk).
*
!*/
!*.md
!*.bpp
!*.sh
!.gitignore
